# BGP Peering on Machine Network
title: BGP Peering on Machine Network {
  near: top-center
  shape: text
  style.font-size: 22
  style.bold: true
}

direction: down

# Switch
switch: "ToR Switch\nAS 65001\n10.0.1.1\nBGP: neighbor default-originate" {
  shape: cylinder
  style.fill: "#1976d2"
  style.font-color: white
}

# OpenShift Cluster
cluster: {
  style.fill: "#f3e5f5"

  masters: {
    label: "Control Plane (No BGP)"
    style.fill: "#7b1fa2"
    style.font-color: white

    grid-rows: 3
    master1: "master-1\n10.0.1.11"
    master2: "master-2\n10.0.1.12"
    master3: "master-3\n10.0.1.13"
  }

  workers_bgp: {
    label: "Workers with BGP (AS 64512)\n✅ Running UDN Workloads\nAdvertising: 192.168.100.0/24"
    style.fill: "#388e3c"
    style.font-color: white

    grid-rows: 3
    worker1: "worker-1\n10.0.1.21\n📦 VMs | 🔷 UDN Pods\n→ Advertises 192.168.100.0/24"
    worker2: "worker-2\n10.0.1.22\n📦 VMs | 🔷 UDN Pods\n→ Advertises 192.168.100.0/24"
    worker3: "worker-3\n10.0.1.23\n📦 VMs | 🔷 UDN Pods\n→ Advertises 192.168.100.0/24"
  }

  workers_no_bgp: {
    label: "Workers without BGP\n❌ Cannot run UDN Workloads"
    style.fill: "#e57373"
    style.font-color: white

    grid-rows: 2
    worker4: "worker-4\n10.0.1.24\n(No UDN)"
    worker5: "worker-5\n10.0.1.25\n(No UDN)"
  }

  udn: {
    label: "User Defined Network (UDN)"
    style.fill: "#fff3e0"
    style.stroke: "#f57c00"
    style.stroke-width: 3

    udn_net: "UDN Network\n192.168.100.0/24\n\nEach BGP worker advertises:\n→ 192.168.100.0/24 to ToR" {
      shape: hexagon
      style.fill: "#ff9800"
      style.font-color: white
    }
  }
}

# Network connection (no BGP)
switch -> cluster.masters: "Network\n(No BGP)" {
  style.stroke: "#9e9e9e"
  style.stroke-width: 2
  style.stroke-dash: 4
}

# BGP Peering (BGP-enabled workers only)
switch -> cluster.workers_bgp: "eBGP\n← 192.168.100.0/24\n→ 0.0.0.0/0 (default)" {
  style.stroke: "#4caf50"
  style.stroke-width: 4
}

# UDN to BGP workers
cluster.udn -> cluster.workers_bgp: "UDN pods/VMs\nrun on BGP workers" {
  style.stroke: "#ff9800"
  style.stroke-width: 2
  style.stroke-dash: 3
}

# Network only (No BGP workers)
switch -> cluster.workers_no_bgp: "Network Only\n(No BGP)" {
  style.stroke: "#9e9e9e"
  style.stroke-width: 2
  style.stroke-dash: 4
}

# Configuration Summary
config: |md
  ## BGP Configuration

  **Network:**
  - Subnet: 10.0.1.0/24
  - All nodes on same CIDR

  **Switch (ToR):**
  - AS 65001
  - Config: neighbor default-originate
  - Receives: 192.168.100.0/24 from each BGP worker
  - Advertises: 0.0.0.0/0 (default route) to workers

  **OpenShift:**
  - Control plane: No BGP
  - Workers (BGP): FRR BGP speakers (AS 64512)
  - Workers (No BGP): Network only, no UDN support
  - Each BGP worker advertises: 192.168.100.0/24
  - Each BGP worker receives: 0.0.0.0/0 (default route)

  **UDN (User Defined Network):**
  - Network: 192.168.100.0/24
  - Advertised by: All BGP-enabled workers
  - ⚠️ **Only runs on BGP-enabled workers**
  - VMs/Pods requiring UDN must be scheduled on BGP workers
| {
  near: bottom-center
  style.fill: "#fff9c4"
}
